4.9 Currently married population aged 12 years and over by LGA, sex
and type of union
In all the LGAs, except Banjul, the proportion of currently married in monogamous union is
higher for females than males. The proportion of the currently married male population in
monogamous unions ranges from 39.5 per cent in Basse to 52.4 per  cent in Banjul. For the
females, the proportion range s from 47.6 per  cent in Banjul to 60.5 per  cent in Basse. For
those in polygamous union, it can be observed that the practice is higher for females in all
LGAs but highest in Basse with 72.5 per cent. (refer to annex, Table E.2)

